   "text": {
    "L1": "Fractions are numbers, so they have places on a number line.",
    "L2": "The bottom number tells how many equal gaps to make from 0 to 1.",
    "L3": "Count gaps, not marks. Four marks between 0 and 1 make five equal gaps.",
    "L4": "So each gap is one fifth. The top number tells how many gaps to count from 0.",
    "L5": "To mark two fifths, count two gaps from 0. That mark is 2/5.",
    "L6": "A fraction can also go beyond 1. If the top number is bigger than the bottom number, it lies past 1.",
    "L7": "For example, 5/4 is one quarter past 1, so it is after 1.",
    "L8": "Now use these ideas to choose where 5/4 belongs."
   },
